WEBVTT

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:19.420
"This is an advance warning."

00:00:19.420 --> 00:00:23.790
"I will be making a call at your residence tonight, Mr. Yashiro,

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.030
to obtain your Angel music box."

00:00:26.030 --> 00:00:28.460
"Cast ye not your pearls before swine!"

00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:33.300
Damn that hoodlum!

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:41.610
Even in light of that, don't we have too many policemen here?

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.180
He's just an ordinary petty thief.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:46.820
We don't consider him to be an ordinary man.

00:00:46.820 --> 00:00:48.190
He's a man of mystery.

00:00:52.180 --> 00:00:55.810
You really think he can sneak past all these guards?

00:00:55.810 --> 00:00:57.540
Preposterous!

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:58.990
He's not made of smoke.

00:01:01.830 --> 00:01:03.040
Smoke bombs?

00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:05.700
Shit.  I can't see!

00:01:07.540 --> 00:01:10.130
Hey you, hold on tight to the music box.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:10.850
Yes, sir!

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.140
Don't lower your guard.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:15.080
He comes and goes like a phantom.

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:17.430
I'm sorry but I can't match your expectations.

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:21.310
I'm human.  Just a regular Joe.

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.060
Damn you!

00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:22.720
You bastard!

00:01:25.790 --> 00:01:26.980
The roof!

00:01:26.980 --> 00:01:27.600
Impossible!

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.980
It's Twenty Faces.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:39.990
Don't let him get away.  Fire!

00:01:42.540 --> 00:01:43.870
Damn it.  Why isn't it firing?

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:50.130
When did he...

00:01:50.130 --> 00:01:53.770
It looks like I've taken the Angel music box, doesn't it?

00:01:56.130 --> 00:01:57.380
He's walking on air...

00:01:57.380 --> 00:01:58.630
Damn that mystery man...

00:02:15.900 --> 00:02:17.720
Wh-What's this?

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:20.910
Don't look!

00:02:22.110 --> 00:02:24.410
Over there!  Open fire!

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:01.840
Extra, extra!  It's Twenty Faces!

00:04:05.890 --> 00:04:08.510
They said that Twenty Faces struck again.

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.270
That's horrible.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:11.520
Oh dear.

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.940
The Yashiro family... That's the cartel that made all that money in the war, right?

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:16.750
How can you defend what that thief did?

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.610
But they did say that no one was injured.

00:04:19.610 --> 00:04:21.440
A scoundrel is a scoundrel.

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:24.030
They say he's a heartless man.

00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.200
And they say he's got twenty different faces!

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:29.410
They say no one's ever seen his real face!

00:04:34.830 --> 00:04:38.500
The man of mystery, Twenty Faces, who stole the Angel music box,

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:41.670
walked across the sky while police watched from below,

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:45.630
and then disappeared as if he vanished into thin air.

00:04:45.630 --> 00:04:50.510
More and more people across the globe are becoming concerned with the audacity of his crimes.

00:04:50.510 --> 00:04:55.440
Inspector Kawada has promised the full resources of the Criminal Investigations Headquarters to help bring him to justice.

00:04:55.440 --> 00:05:00.980
Furthermore, secret assets that were acquired illegally during the war by Mr. Yashiro Taizou...

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:04.110
...were exposed in the course of this crime.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:06.320
The authorities have promised stern punishments for—

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:10.200
Chizuko-san, shall we go have some tea?

00:05:12.950 --> 00:05:15.960
Here you go.

00:05:15.960 --> 00:05:19.670
Supposedly, this is the tea that the British royal family drinks.

00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:23.550
The chocolates were brought back from France by a friend of mine.

00:05:23.550 --> 00:05:25.550
Well now, drink up.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:05:59.620
Why must she...

00:05:59.620 --> 00:06:02.440
She's at that rebellious age.

00:06:02.440 --> 00:06:03.680
Kawai.

00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:05.050
Yes, sir.

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.600
Young mistress, it's Kawai.

00:06:17.600 --> 00:06:18.980
It's open.

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:28.740
I took the liberty of brewing you some fresh tea.

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:46.630
You certainly are reading some rather difficult books for your age, young mistress.

00:06:46.630 --> 00:06:48.840
They're not difficult at all.

00:06:48.840 --> 00:06:51.130
I just read them over and over until I understand them.

00:06:51.130 --> 00:06:54.180
Shall I order you some young women's magazines?

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.010
If you're done with the tea, then leave.

00:06:56.010 --> 00:06:59.640
Your father and mother are very worried about you.

00:06:59.640 --> 00:07:01.060
I said leave.

00:07:01.060 --> 00:07:02.440
As you wish.

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:20.210
I want to...

00:07:20.210 --> 00:07:22.370
...get away from this place.

00:07:50.320 --> 00:07:53.160
Your mother worked hard today.

00:07:53.160 --> 00:07:54.660
It looks great.

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.990
Your mother made all this by herself.

00:07:57.500 --> 00:08:01.040
Now, eat up before it gets cold.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:16.030
Thank you for the meal.

00:08:16.030 --> 00:08:16.800
Chizuko!

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:21.020
It looks like we've been too easy on you.

00:08:21.770 --> 00:08:22.640
Honey...

00:08:22.640 --> 00:08:24.810
We're going to eat together as a family.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:26.020
There!

00:08:26.020 --> 00:08:29.270
Hold your spoon properly!

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.990
Now eat!

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.450
Don't force her, honey...

00:08:37.660 --> 00:08:38.990
I'm sorry.

00:08:38.990 --> 00:08:40.870
I don't know what got into me.

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:44.870
I hate you.  I hate both of you!

00:08:46.880 --> 00:08:50.050
I hate this family!

00:08:58.760 --> 00:09:01.850
Young mistress, it's Kawai.

00:09:01.850 --> 00:09:03.390
Come in.

00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:08.900
You must be hungry.  I went out and bought this for you.

00:09:08.900 --> 00:09:11.400
We'll keep it secret from your father.

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:17.660
You're reading another detective novel, aren't you?

00:09:17.660 --> 00:09:18.950
Is it interesting?

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:23.500
I'm not reading it because it's interesting.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:27.370
You have a bit of chocolate on your face, young mistress.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:43.270
You're Inspector Kawada, correct?

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:47.730
What kind of person is Twenty Faces?

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:49.060
No idea, no idea.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.230
I've never gotten a good look at his face.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:53.780
Well, in any case, I'm very busy.  Go on home.

00:09:54.900 --> 00:09:57.110
I'm pretty busy myself,

00:09:57.110 --> 00:09:59.170
looking for information on that guy.

00:09:59.170 --> 00:10:00.910
Just who are you?

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:02.950
I'm a selfish rascal named Tiger.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.950
Tiger?  You bastard...

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:09.830
You're going to tell me everything you know about Twenty Faces.

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:10.710
If you don't...

00:10:15.260 --> 00:10:16.720
I'm going to eat you!

00:10:21.220 --> 00:10:24.720
Madame, this letter was in the mailbox.

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:27.230
There's no return address written on it.

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.140
Leave it over there for me, please.

00:10:29.140 --> 00:10:33.230
Oh, and also, take this juice to Chizuko's room.

00:10:36.570 --> 00:10:39.740
Your mother prepared this juice for you.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:45.080
I will leave it here for you.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:48.250
Kawai-san, do you know about Twenty Faces?

00:10:48.250 --> 00:10:51.250
I've heard that he is a rather formidable thief.

00:10:51.250 --> 00:10:54.000
They say he never hurts anyone.

00:10:54.000 --> 00:10:59.010
That may be true, but since he is performing criminal acts, he may be forced to one day.

00:10:59.010 --> 00:11:02.260
He travels all over the world to do his work.

00:11:02.260 --> 00:11:05.760
He's a rogue no matter where he goes.

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:08.770
I want to be able to do that too.

00:11:08.770 --> 00:11:12.020
But more importantly, you must be hungry.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:14.020
Would you like me to go out and buy you something again?

00:11:14.020 --> 00:11:17.210
I want to...

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:19.030
...get away from this place.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:21.280
Young mistress!

00:11:21.280 --> 00:11:23.780
Someone!  The young mistress is ill!

00:11:23.780 --> 00:11:25.370
Please call a doctor!

00:11:25.870 --> 00:11:28.290
Somewhere else...

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:31.120
I am not sure what caused her to collapse.

00:11:31.120 --> 00:11:33.290
I'll come back in the morning to check on her.

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:34.540
We appreciate that.

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.050
It's because of my selfish behavior towards her before.

00:11:38.050 --> 00:11:41.050
I even forced her to eat against her will.

00:11:42.470 --> 00:11:44.720
How is Chizuko doing?

00:11:44.720 --> 00:11:48.060
I made some porridge to provide her with some nourishment.

00:11:48.060 --> 00:11:49.680
Chizuko.

00:11:57.110 --> 00:11:59.070
Since you went to the effort to make it, I'll eat it.

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:02.030
My!  I'm glad.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:10.080
Because I've been helping you cook since I was a little girl,

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:13.080
I've come to understand the flavors of lots of different foods.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:16.210
At first, I just thought it tasted a bit odd.

00:12:16.210 --> 00:12:19.500
But I knew I shouldn't tell you that, so I kept my mouth shut.

00:12:19.500 --> 00:12:20.380
However...

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:24.340
...after reading so many detective novels, I figured it out.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:29.970
You've been drugging my food bit by bit, so that even the doctor wouldn't notice.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:33.640
But it would better if I didn't know.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:36.600
They didn't say what I should do in the novels.

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:41.990
If I still didn't know, I could go to be with my mother and father in Heaven.

00:12:41.990 --> 00:12:45.360
There's no one I can trust here.

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:47.990
Not you, Uncle, or you, Auntie.

00:12:47.990 --> 00:12:49.740
You're being silly, Chizuko.

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:53.000
You're the precious child that my big brother left behind.

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.620
Exactly.  We love you as if you were our own daughter.

00:12:56.620 --> 00:12:58.630
Now go on and eat.

00:12:58.630 --> 00:13:01.130
You need your nutrition.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:04.260
You're in the direct line to inherit.

00:13:04.260 --> 00:13:07.390
Sooner or later, the house, the company – all of it will become your responsibility.

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:11.640
As your guardians, we just want you to have a wonderful upbringing.

00:13:11.640 --> 00:13:13.140
No!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:19.770
Pig feed...

00:13:21.150 --> 00:13:22.250
Kawai!

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:27.490
...is only fit for pigs.

00:13:30.410 --> 00:13:31.660
That bottle!

00:13:33.410 --> 00:13:35.210
If you're going to boast about your cooking,

00:13:35.210 --> 00:13:37.000
then you should be the one eating it.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.750
We can even put in some more of your favorite spice.

00:13:40.750 --> 00:13:43.130
A disguise?  Y-You couldn't be...

00:13:43.130 --> 00:13:44.340
Twenty Faces?

00:13:44.340 --> 00:13:45.380
...Twenty Faces?

00:13:45.380 --> 00:13:47.380
This is he?

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:52.510
My job is taking treasure away from pigs.

00:13:54.140 --> 00:13:57.310
You must agree with me that the greatest treasure left in this house...

00:13:57.310 --> 00:13:59.900
...is Chizuko-kun, do you not?

00:14:01.400 --> 00:14:03.860
Chizuko-kun, what do you want to do?

00:14:03.860 --> 00:14:06.860
I-I want to get away from this place.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:08.110
No...

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:09.610
I want to go with you!

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:10.620
Chizuko!

00:14:16.540 --> 00:14:17.710
Come then.

00:14:28.880 --> 00:14:30.260
Shall we go...

00:14:30.260 --> 00:14:31.890
...to the world outside?

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:37.520
Chizuko!

00:14:38.090 --> 00:14:40.020
Oops, I almost forgot.

00:14:40.900 --> 00:14:44.520
It looks like I've taken the family heirloom, the Anastasia Ruby.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:49.530
But it seems rather insignificant in light of the other treasure I've just received.

00:14:51.910 --> 00:14:54.620
S-Someone call the police!

00:14:54.620 --> 00:14:55.540
The ruby—

00:14:55.540 --> 00:14:59.120
No, Chizuko's been kidnapped by Twenty Faces!

00:15:15.470 --> 00:15:18.270
Our quiet night is about to be ruined.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.480
Chizuko-kun, it's going to get a little bumpy.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:32.660
Mister...

00:15:32.660 --> 00:15:33.820
They're fine.

00:15:33.820 --> 00:15:35.240
That little accident won't hurt them.

00:15:59.720 --> 00:16:02.060
Mister, there are at least nine patrol cars.

00:16:02.060 --> 00:16:04.350
Pull over, Twenty Faces!

00:16:04.350 --> 00:16:06.560
Give it up.  You're not getting away!

00:16:08.320 --> 00:16:09.570
Perfect timing.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.250
Damn it!

00:16:29.250 --> 00:16:31.380
What are you doing?  Go around!  Around!

00:16:34.880 --> 00:16:36.930
Are you safe, Boss?

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:39.640
Yeah.  That was great timing, Skipper, Ken.

00:16:40.470 --> 00:16:42.450
Boss, who's this brat—

00:16:42.450 --> 00:16:44.140
Err, I mean, this young lady?

00:16:44.140 --> 00:16:46.650
I'll introduce you later.  Let's hurry.

00:16:48.900 --> 00:16:51.570
Hey, what's your name?

00:16:51.570 --> 00:16:53.950
Chizuko.  It's Mikamo Chizuko.

00:16:53.950 --> 00:16:54.870
Chizuko?

00:16:54.870 --> 00:16:55.930
OK, Chiko it is.

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:56.410
How old are you?

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:57.950
Eleven.

00:16:57.950 --> 00:17:00.410
You can relax.  They're comrades of mine.

00:17:00.410 --> 00:17:03.960
Yup.  And there's a lot more of us at the hideout.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:07.920
They share in the ups and downs of the work we do together.

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:09.130
They're family.

00:17:09.130 --> 00:17:10.440
Family?

00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.470
Heh, I like the sound of that!

00:17:12.470 --> 00:17:16.030
If the Boss is the father, then the Skipper here is his stubborn old man!

00:17:16.030 --> 00:17:20.100
I'll pass on having a grandson like you, thanks.

00:17:29.360 --> 00:17:32.400
Nice to meet you, Twenty Faces-kun.

00:17:32.400 --> 00:17:33.360
I'm Tiger.

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:34.820
Tiger, huh?

00:17:34.820 --> 00:17:37.360
Even your name separates you from the rest of us humans.

00:17:37.360 --> 00:17:40.990
I'm interested in the treasures that you have.

00:17:40.990 --> 00:17:43.720
Trying to get a piece of our action?

00:17:43.720 --> 00:17:44.660
That's pretty clever.

00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.060
So that was Tiger, huh?

00:18:08.060 --> 00:18:11.400
Only a fool would try to steal the Boss's treasure.

00:18:11.400 --> 00:18:14.480
We've been having more and more encounters like that of late.

00:18:14.480 --> 00:18:17.320
We've been a little showy with our work.  That makes more enemies.

00:18:17.320 --> 00:18:19.860
Oh, well.  That's always the case.

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:20.990
Always?

00:18:20.990 --> 00:18:24.080
These are daily occurrences for those of us who dwell in the night.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:27.580
However, we can't just sit around being afraid of the darkness.

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:33.420
In order to survive, what's important is to watch, listen, and think carefully.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:34.840
Just like you've been doing.

00:18:42.760 --> 00:18:43.890
What was that?!

00:19:01.860 --> 00:19:03.910
Damn him.  I'll teach him a lesson!

00:19:05.790 --> 00:19:08.330
Are you going to become a murderer too now, Ken?

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:10.290
Are you prepared for the consequences?

00:19:13.460 --> 00:19:14.290
you won't sleep at night.

00:19:37.440 --> 00:19:38.630
They're here.

00:19:44.030 --> 00:19:45.580
Boss, hurry up!

00:19:46.450 --> 00:19:47.990
Ken, Skipper...

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:48.670
Right!

00:19:51.580 --> 00:19:54.210
Are you OK with high places?

00:19:54.210 --> 00:19:55.460
Yes!

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:29.040
One of those lights is the house that has controlled you all these years.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:33.250
But when you see it from up here, the world seems rather small, doesn't it?

00:20:33.250 --> 00:20:37.040
We're going to be leaving this country in a short while.

00:20:37.040 --> 00:20:39.760
Will you come and see the world, Chiko?

00:20:39.760 --> 00:20:40.760
Yes!

00:20:42.260 --> 00:20:43.760
You finally smiled, eh?
